    "id": "p69-q3",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "Show that\n$${}^{n}C_k=\\frac{n-k+1}{k}\\,{}^{n}C_{k-1}.$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac{n-k+1}{k}\\,{}^{n}C_{k-1}=\\dfrac{n!}{k!(n-k)!}={}^{n}C_k$.",
      "worked": "For integers $1\\leq k\\leq n$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\mathrm{LHS}&=\\frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!}.\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}\\mathrm{RHS}&=\\frac{n-k+1}{k}\\times\\frac{n!}{(k-1)!(n-k+1)!}\\\\&=\\frac{(n-k+1)\\times n!}{k(k-1)!(n-k+1)!}\\\\&=\\frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!}\\\\&=\\mathrm{LHS}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 35
  },
